    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`CityOwnerCounter.java`** (new) \u2014 a small `@Component` with a single responsibility: count existing owners in a given city (case-insensitive, in-memory). It mirrors the existing `NamesakeCounter` exactly, reusing `ClinicService.findAllOwners()` rather than introducing new persistence logic.\n\n2. **`CustomerCodeGenerator.java`** \u2014 kept as a pure formatter. `generate` now takes `(city, lastName, cityOwnerCount)` and emits `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where the 3-letter prefix logic is factored into a shared `prefix(...)` helper (used for both city and last name) instead of duplicated.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 injects `CityOwnerCounter` and passes the city plus the per-city count to the generator. The membership number is untouched: since it's derived from `customerCode` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), it is automatically rebuilt on the new format.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (matching `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nFor a fresh, unique city the sequence starts at `0001`; owners added to the same city increment it (`0002`, `0003`, \u2026), since `count` returns the number already present and the generator adds one.",
